	(text "MOTOR SWITCH (record section 4). Back-to-back N-FETs, common source, charge pump (TPS4811 integrated 12 V pump: DC on, no bootstrap droop).\nOpen = open both ways: back-drive never reaches the board, which is why the shunt sizes for the powered 6.8 W case.\nMOTOR_EN floats during P4 boot/reset: R4 pulldown + the chip's internal INP pulldown = off (hard requirement, section 4).\nINA_ALERT_N on EN/UVLO: INA228 over-current/over-power/over-temp limits open the switch in hardware, no MCU (section 12, sd-4k1.31).\nPRE-CHARGE: the drive's input measures 150 uF (operator DMM 2026-09-22, hw-x65), empty whenever the switch is open; a user bank per the 1000 uF recommendation (section 6) adds to it.\n  Closing Q3/Q4 onto it unlimited is a hundreds-of-amps spike that trips ISCP in ~1.2 us. At 150 uF: 0.1 J; R7 = 100R gives ~75 ms to charge, 0.36 A peak.\n  Q5 + R7 from the G pin pre-charge it first (PRECHARGE_EN, then MOTOR_EN): this is why the L variant (TPS48111) was picked.\nR3 + IWRN/ISCP: the chip's own two-level over-current trip, independent of the INA. TODO(detailing): thresholds, R7 value, FET choice, TVS on MOTOR_V+."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 165 0)
